{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness","id":1448987,"title":"What are the extra side effects of the Lasombra's V20 Clan Weakness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-19T07:50:41-07:00","id":1448987,"title":"What are the extra side effects of the Lasombra's V20 Clan Weakness?","content":"Off the top of my head, there's the psychological toll of no longer remembering your own face and not readily noticing a change to your appearance, should such a change take place without your knowledge.<br /> <br /> Is there any technology, particularly common everyday tech, that uses mirrors and reflections? Or out of date technology that used to? (Not like, &quot;Lasombra can't function in the 21st century&quot;, so much as &quot;Lasombra are occasionally inconvenienced&quot;.)<br /> <br /> I seem to recall something about automatic doors using reflections in mirrors to recognise when somebody is in front of them, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> The curse doesn't exactly follow scientific logic, but if the curse is because they're sort of walking black holes that absorb light into nothingness rather than reflecting it, could that have any other consequences beyond a lack of reflection?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-19-2021, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T08:15:18-07:00","id":1448988,"title":"","content":"Ironically enough with the Lasombras connection to the sea, periscopes wouldn't show them to the viewer. Even modern periscopes use the same basic design of two angled mirrors to see around corners or up through the water.<br /> <br /> V20 just states reflections are nullified, earlier versions also suggested that cameras had problems recording Lasombra as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:00:26-07:00","id":1448998,"title":"","content":"Not quite answering your question, here, but for \u201cscientific logic,\u201d I would have had the Lasombra affected by silver, as a counterbalance to the Outer Darkness they tap into. Historically, silver had an adverse affect on all supernatural being, not just werewolves.<br /> <br /> Since early mirrors and photography used silver in their creation, the lack of reflection would be attributed to this. Admittedly, that would be much less of a nuisance in modern times, to be sure, but coupled with additional damage or other negative physical effects from silver would be an effective clan weakness that would stand the test of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:04:18-07:00","id":1448999,"title":"","content":"Yeah, silver makes much more sense as a Lasombra weakness than this &quot;can't use tech&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:42:22-07:00","id":1449007,"title":"","content":"The way I interpret the weakness is that Lasombra are so tied to shadows/the Abyss/essence of darkness (aka total absence of light) that they don't produce light. Reflections are made of light, so the Lasombra are cut off from them. (The human eye can perceive them for, I dunno, reasons. Vampire logic doesn't care about science.) Phones, audio recording, laptops, whatever, they should all work fine.<br /> It's mirrors that are the problem, and by extension aformentioned periscopes, cameras and possibly automatic doors. I wonder if this extends to lenses like glasses? That would be, uh, strange.<br /> <br /> I don't get V5's weakness, frankly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:45:16-07:00","id":1449009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1448988#post1448988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically enough with the Lasombras connection to the sea, periscopes wouldn't show them to the viewer. Even modern periscopes use the same basic design of two angled mirrors to see around corners or up through the water.<br /> <br /> V20 just states reflections are nullified, earlier versions also suggested that cameras had problems recording Lasombra as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had the most ridiculous realisation that if you could get a Tzimisce to fleshcraft a whole ship out of failed Lasombra fledglings, you'd essentially have a ship totally invisible to submarines' periscopes.<br /> <br /> Build a car from them (...somehow) and you'll never upset a speed camera","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-19-2021, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T11:13:35-07:00","id":1449015,"title":"","content":"This again.<br /> It's really, really awful when you think about it enough. You're going to become a control freak.<br /> <br /> First, modern cities are filled with reflective surfaces; Large shopping windows, hundreds of cars with rear-view mirrors, wet roads illuminated by the lights of the street. Either you stick to the right streets on dry days or you'll spend your time looking over your shoulder wondering if anyone of a hundred people noticed that you don't have a reflection. Maybe you'll have to trouble yourself with taking care of a few because better safe than sorry. You'll want to take control as a result; ensure the nightclubs you haunt aren't loaded with mirrors, that you've got your own car service with people you trust because there's absolutely no way you can just take a vehicle casually. Your enemies know you have this weakness, and they'll do their best to insert MORE mirrors at the places you depend on. The hunters tipped off to your weakness can confirm you're a vampire in a crowd from a mile off. Lastly, if someone draws a cock on your face just before you rise in the evening, you're going to find out a lot later than anyone else would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T11:33:55-07:00","id":1449018,"title":"","content":"Back when they first created the Lasombra and Tzimisce, they seemed to want them to be the Dracula clans. One was Lugosi Dracula, and the other was Mexican Dracula. (Mexican Dracula is widely considered the superior of the two early Dracula movies, interestingly) So they gave them the classic weaknesses of no reflection and resting in their native soil.<br /> <br /> However, they noticed that Lasombra players were using their weakness as an advantage, as a way to stealth past security cameras. And they haaaated that. Everything about being a vampire is supposed to be unrelenting misery. Heaven forbid your weakness have even a tiny, situational upside. So they've been fiddling with it ever since.<br /> <br /> This is just the latest fiddle attempt, and boy did they go overboard. It's now an absolutely horrific weakness, especially for a High Clan. It feels more like the sort of weakness that might have fit the Gangrel if they hadn't been given the weakness they actually were given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T11:43:00-07:00","id":1449020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449009#post1449009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just had the most ridiculous realisation that if you could get a Tzimisce to fleshcraft a whole ship out of failed Lasombra fledglings, you'd essentially have a ship totally invisible to submarines' periscopes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint, if they cast no <i>reflection</i> they should be invisible to radar, sonar, and lidar (the least arguable of the three) as well.<br /> <br /> Which if you think about it, a Lasombra with Animalism and a herd of ghouled bats could be the <i>ultimate</i> troll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 05-19-2021, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:41:29-07:00","id":1449030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449018#post1449018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, they noticed that Lasombra players were using their weakness as an advantage, as a way to stealth past security cameras. And they haaaated that. Everything about being a vampire is supposed to be unrelenting misery. Heaven forbid your weakness have even a tiny, situational upside. So they've been fiddling with it ever since.<br /> <br /> This is just the latest fiddle attempt, and boy did they go overboard. It's now an absolutely horrific weakness, especially for a High Clan. It feels more like the sort of weakness that might have fit the Gangrel if they hadn't been given the weakness they actually were given.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the V5 weakness is also, again, because of the decision to make the new discipline Oblivion.<br /> The Abyss, if I recall correctly, was a literal living darkness, so no light. Oblivion is literal nothingness, so not only is there no light but no sound or other sensory infomation. So now not only can light detection-based technology (like cameras) not work, now phones don't work.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hang on, I just checked Obtenebration. Shroud of Night muffles sound a little bit. Hmm. Still don't feel like these two should be exactly the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-19-2021, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T22:52:06-07:00","id":1449093,"title":"","content":"My headcanon for why legendary vampires didn't have reflections (or shadows, in some stories) was that rather than being reanimated corpses they were really solid ghosts. In VtM that works with Lasombra drawing on creepy extradimensional forces that may alter the substance of their bodies or move them &quot;out of phase&quot; with the world of the living, so that they don't behave quite like matter in certain respects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T00:06:06-07:00","id":1449097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449009#post1449009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had the most ridiculous realisation that if you could get a Tzimisce to fleshcraft a whole ship out of failed Lasombra fledglings, you'd essentially have a ship totally invisible to submarines' periscopes.<br /> <br /> Build a car from them (...somehow) and you'll never upset a speed camera</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, the ship would be invisible, but all the other occupants who are not Lasombra would be fully visible to the admittedly confused viewer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T00:39:35-07:00","id":1449098,"title":"","content":"From a practical standpoint I find it annoying that you basically have to do a 2 hour discussion round for just this aspect any time you want to include a lasombra player character. It's better than someone feeling cheated 3 session in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T16:29:04-07:00","id":1449155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449097#post1449097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no, the ship would be invisible, but all the other occupants who are not Lasombra would be fully visible to the admittedly confused viewer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until whomever is on the submarine decides to ping it, then your cunning stealth boat transforms into a slapstick comedy machine.<br /> <br /> That would be an <i>assload</i> of (bashing, hell maybe even lethal) damage, and probably a serious contender for the Most Creative Vampire Kill award.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T16:47:24-07:00","id":1449159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449155#post1449155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until whomever is on the submarine decides to ping it, then your cunning stealth boat transforms into a slapstick comedy machine.<br /> <br /> That would be an <i>assload</i> of (bashing, hell maybe even lethal) damage, and probably a serious contender for the Most Creative Vampire Kill award.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if you teach the Lasombra-boat materials fortitude? (And don't lobotomize them in the building process so that they can use it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-20-2021, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T19:33:36-07:00","id":1449414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449097#post1449097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no, the ship would be invisible, but all the other occupants who are not Lasombra would be fully visible to the admittedly confused viewer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their eyes would be visible you mean. I mean if you go through all of that trouble for the boat, how would you not have Lasombra suits for the crew?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T23:48:40-07:00","id":1449427,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine there is an identical thread exactly like this one on a message board in the World of Darkness in which Tzimisce are spitballing for new ideas on what to do with their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T13:34:05-07:00","id":1449486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448987-what-are-the-extra-side-effects-of-the-lasombra-s-v20-clan-weakness?p=1449414#post1449414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their eyes would be visible you mean. I mean if you go through all of that trouble for the boat, how would you not have Lasombra suits for the crew?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, the suits would be invisible, not the people wearing them. Less cloak of invisibility, more emperors new clothes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}